claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> On Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:32:11 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
>>> +  # Mail state that must survive a rebuild.
>>> +  exec.prepare += "install -d -m 0755 /jails/data/lab-mail/mail";
>>
>> I don't think this should create the dir on the host. Operator should
>> create it before starting the jail, just like the secrets dir.
>
> Agreed. v9 drops every install -d of a host path from jail.conf, here
> and in 4/6 and 5/6, and keeps only the mkdir of the mountpoint inside
> the jail root, as the secrets mount does. The README setup section
> will give the operator one block that creates /jails/data/lab-mail/mail
> and its maildir, mbsync and dovecot subdirectories with their owners
> and modes, beside the secrets block. The line "The jail creates it on
> start" goes, and spec.org gets a line that the operator creates the
> data dirs, so the spec and the patches agree.
>
> If the operator forgets, the nullfs mount has no source and the jail
> should fail to start, which names the missing path. That is inference
> from jail(8); I have not run it on beastie.
>
> I am holding v9 until you answer the encoding tool request on 3/6 and
> the IMAP question on 5/6 and 6/6, since either answer may change those
> patches. My replies to both are in this thread.

I responded, I think it's good to go now.
